message.content:
Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows a “card” element rotating around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy‑paste the HTML and CSS into your own file or into an online editor such as CodePen / JSFiddle.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card on Hover</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣ Basic reset & layout ---------- */
body {
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    min-height:100vh;
    margin:0;
    background:#f0f0f0;
    font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣ Card container (perspective) ---------- */
.card-wrapper {
    perspective: 1000px;          /* gives depth to the 3D effect */
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣ The card itself ---------- */
.card {
    width:260px;
    height:160px;
    border-radius:12px;
    overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(0,0,0,.15);
    background:#fff;
    cursor:pointer;
    transition:transform .6s ease; /* smooth rotation */
    transform-style:preserve-3d;   /* keep children in 3D space */
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣ Front & back faces ---------- */
.card::before,
.card::after {
    content:"";
    position:absolute;
    inset:0;
    backface-visibility:hidden;   /* hide backside when rotated */
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    font-size:1.4rem;
    font-weight:bold;
    color:#fff;
}

.card::before {            /* front face */
    background:#3498db;
    z-index:2;
}

.card::after {             /* back face */
    background:#e74c3c;
    transform:rotateY(180deg); /* start rotated so it's hidden */
}

/* ---------- 5️⃣ Hover effect ---------- */
.card:hover {
    transform:rotateY(180deg); /* flip the card */
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <!-- Front content -->
        <div class="front">Front</div>
        <!-- Back content -->
        <div class="back">Back</div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens |
|------|--------------|
| **1** | Basic page styling – center the card on the screen. |
| **2** | `perspective` on the wrapper gives the 3D effect. |
| **3** | The `.card` has `transform-style: preserve-3d` so its pseudo‑elements stay in 3D space. |
| **4** | Two pseudo‑elements (`::before` and `::after`) act as the front and back faces. `backface-visibility:hidden` hides the back when it’s turned away. |
| **5** | On hover, the card rotates 180° around the Y‑axis, revealing the back face. |

You can replace the pseudo‑elements with real `<div>` children if you prefer, or add images/text inside the `.front` and `.back` elements. Adjust colors, size, or rotation axis (`rotateX`, `rotateZ`) to fit your design.
